@page "/docs/primitives/merge-props"

<DocsPage Title="Merge Props" Description="Merges attributes the way the primitives do: event handlers chain, classes join and styles append.">
    <p>
        Merging sets of attributes means handling event handlers, <code>class</code> and
        <code>style</code>. Here it's two helpers, one for each place you need it.
    </p>
    <DocsHeading Title="MergeProps" />
    <p>
        <code>MergeProps.Merge</code> merges sets of attributes. Later sets win, except that event handlers all run (the later
        set's first), <code>class</code> values are joined, and <code>style</code> declarations are appended, so the later
        set's win. Use it when a <code>Render</code> fragment needs a part's attributes and your own on one element:
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@MergeCode" />
    <DocsHeading Title="AttributeBuilder" />
    <p>
        <code>AttributeBuilder</code> builds the attributes a part renders: the ones its author wrote (<code>class</code>,
        <code>style</code>, <code>data-testid</code>, handlers...) overlaid with the part's own. The part's values win,
        except that both event handlers run (the author's first), the author's <code>style</code> comes after the part's, and
        <code>Default</code> values apply only when the author didn't set one. A null value removes the attribute, and
        <code>Flag</code> renders a presence attribute such as <code>data-open</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Here the button gets <code>type="button"</code> unless its author set a type, <code>data-pressed=""</code> only while
        it's pressed, and an <code>onclick</code> that runs after the author's.
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@BuilderCode" Language="csharp" />
    <p>See <a href="/docs/primitives/use-render">Use Render</a> for building a whole part with it.</p>
    <DocsHeading Title="API Reference" />
    <PartReference Type="typeof(MergeProps)" />
    <PartReference Type="typeof(AttributeBuilder)" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string MergeCode = """
        <MenuItem>
            <Render Context="item">
                <a @attributes="MergeProps.Merge(item.Attributes, _link)">Settings</a>
            </Render>
        </MenuItem>

        @code {
            private readonly Dictionary<string, object> _link = new() { ["href"] = "/settings", ["class"] = "menu-link" };
        }
        """;

    private const string BuilderCode = """
        protected override void BuildAttributes(AttributeBuilder attributes) => attributes
            .Default("type", "button")
            .Set("aria-pressed", Pressed ? "true" : "false")
            .Flag("data-pressed", Pressed)
            .Set("onclick", _onClick);
        """;
}
